Network  Disk (ND) Protocol server is a server which supports the
Sun Network Disk (ND) Protocol.  This protocol  was  designed  by
Sun before they designed ND simply makes the raw blocks of a disk
available  to network clients.  Contrast this with the true name‐
space and file  abstractions  that  provides.   The  only  reason
you’re  likely to encounter ND nowadays is if you have an old Sun
2 machine, like the 2/120 or 2/50.  The Sun 2 PROMs can only  use
ND  to  boot over the network.  (Later, the Sun 3 PROMs would use
